Subject: Plug-in: metal_trace=frame, a whole frame as the driver received it and the GPU ran it

The frame trace written for the study of how iOS draws
(dev-notes/investigacion/19-como-dibuja-ios.md, section 5.3), as its two patches
apply to this branch: touching /var/tmp/metal.trace has the next K command
buffers written whole to /var/tmp/metal-trace-<pid>-<n>.txt -- each command
buffer with its times, each encoder with its attachments and their actions,
each texture with where its memory is, each pipeline with where each stage's
code came from, its constants and its blending, each draw with its area, the
box of its transformed vertices, its bindings and whether it was drawn, and
each of the core's passes with its mode, tiles and GPU time. With the mode off
it costs one boolean a command buffer. Its reader is trace-frame.py, kept with
the study outside this tree.

The core gains hakios_metal_program_fs_traits (which colour attachments a
fragment stage reads by framebuffer fetch, and whether it can discard), which
the trace looks up by name.


